(1J The Chancellor may, upon the recommendation of the Review Panel,remove any person from the membership of the Board of Governors onthe ground that such Person:(a) has become of unsound rnind; or(b) has become incapacitated to function as member of the Board ofGovernors; or
(c) has been convicted by a court of lawfor an offence involvingmoral turpitude; or has absented himself from twoconsecutive meetings without just cause; or(d) Has been guilty of mlsconduct, including use of position.forpersonal advantage of any kind, or gross inefficlency in theperformance of functionsThe Chancellor shall remove any person from the membership of theBoard of Governors on a resolution calling for t}re removal of suchperson supported by at least three-fourths of the membership of theBoard ofGovernors:
{2)
provided that before passing such a resolution the Board ofGovernors shall provide themember concerned a fair hearing.provicled further that the provisiops of this section shall not be applicable to the ViceChancellor in his capacity as a member of the Board of GovernOrs.13 Vice C ancellor:[1) There shall be a Vice Chancellor of the Institute who shall be an eminentacademician or a distinguished administrator and shall be appointed onsuch terms and conditions as may be prescribed.(Z) The Vice Chancellor shall be the chief executive officer of the Instituteresponsible for all administrative and academic functions of the Instituteand for ensuring that the provisibns of the Act, Statutes, Regulations andRules are faithfully observed to promote the general efficiency and goodorder of the Institute. The Vice Chancellor shall have all powers prescribed: for this purpose, including administrative control over the officers,teachers, and other employees of the Institute.(3) The Vice Chancellor shalli if present, be entitled to attend any meeting ofany Authority or body of the Institute.(4) The Vice Chancellor may, in an emergency that in his opinion requiresimmediate action ordinarlly not in the competence of the Vice.Chancellor,take such action and forward, within seventy-two hours, a report of the
