the Government, as the Chancellor may, from time to time, nominate' Themember so nominated shall be the convener of the Board of Governors.(71 Unless otherwise prescribed by this Act, all decisions of the Board ofGovernors shall be raken based on the opinion of a majority of the membersprcsent. In thc cvcnt of the membcrs being evenly divided on any matterthc person presiding over the meeting shali lrave a casting vote.(B) The quorum for a meeting of the Board of Governors shall be nrro thirds ofits membership, a fraction being counted as one'25, Powersand functionsoft e Board ofGovernors'-(i ) Thc Board of Govcrnors slrall have the power of general supervision over the Instit'uteand shall hold thc Vice Chanccllor and the Authorities accountable for all the functions ofthc Institr.rre. The Board of Governors shall have all powers of the Institute not expresslyvcsted in an Authoriry or officer by the Act and all other powers not expressly mentionedby this Act that are necessary for the performance of its functions,
